<title>USA: Concurrent Computer Q3 March 29 net rises.</title>
<headline>Concurrent Computer Q3 March 29 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>FORT LAUDERDALE, Fla. 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>CONCURRENT COMPUTER CORP</p>
<p>			    Three Months Ended    Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>		     3/29/97  3/31/96  12/27/96  3/29/97  3/31/96</p>
<p>Revenue	     $	    $	     $	    $</p>
<p>   Equipment	16,440   13,831   12,870    42,196   35,696</p>
<p>   Maintenance    12,215   12,342   13,755    40,841   41,412</p>
<p> Total		28,655   26,173   26,625    83,037   77,108</p>
<p> Gross Margin     13,362   10,890   12,609    38,123   32,682</p>
<p> EPS		    0.05     0.02     0.06	0.02  ( 0.19)</p>
<p> EPS*		   0.05     0.02     0.01	0.08   (0.14)</p>
<p>NOTE: EPS* excludes transition and restructuring expense, CyberGuard stock Loss and other non-recurring charges.</p>
<p>Profit year-to-date for fiscal year 1997 is $0.9 million, or $0.02 per share, including a loss of $1.9 million for the revaluation of CyberGuard Corp stock, compared with a loss of ($5.7 million), or ($0.19) per share, for the same period year-to-date.</p>
<p>Sales and profit were adversely affected by approximately ($0.9) million and ($0.1) million due to the strength of the U.S. dollar.</p>
